WEBVTT

00:09.142 --> 00:17.183
As a white, crescent moon overlooks the town

00:17.183 --> 00:25.181
From within a pale, blue maze
devilish things begin to stir

00:32.699 --> 00:36.503
Boy, here in this sinful world

00:36.503 --> 00:39.506
Believing, dreaming

00:39.506 --> 00:43.343
We are searching

00:43.343 --> 00:48.474
For the place to which souls should aspire

00:50.283 --> 00:58.691
Ah, how much profound darkness
must we turn to light

00:58.691 --> 01:03.263
For the color of the world to change?

01:03.263 --> 01:05.932
Ah, surely someday

01:05.932 --> 01:14.207
Ah, how many profound riddles must we solve

01:14.207 --> 01:19.167
For the door to paradise to open?

01:20.713 --> 01:27.346
Let's begin our journey

01:55.648 --> 01:56.774
I have a premonition.

02:12.265 --> 02:18.033
The 1st Night
Presenting: The Mythical Detective!

02:47.133 --> 02:48.930
Ouch!

02:49.869 --> 02:51.530
Darn it...

03:03.383 --> 03:04.884
Huh? A ghost?!

03:04.884 --> 03:07.580
Yup. They say it haunts the clock tower.

03:08.388 --> 03:10.583
Awesome! A strange mystery!

03:10.890 --> 03:13.193
There she goes with that
"strange mystery" thing again.

03:13.193 --> 03:15.753
You sure love these kinds of
stories, don't you, Mayura?

03:16.262 --> 03:18.598
Hey, what kind of ghost is it?

03:18.598 --> 03:19.966
Does it do spirit knocking?

03:19.966 --> 03:23.002
Or maybe it throws things around
like a poltergeist!

03:23.002 --> 03:23.169
Tuesday
Daily Duties
Izumi Takaya
Or maybe it throws things around
like a poltergeist!

03:23.169 --> 03:26.539
Tuesday
Daily Duties
Izumi Takaya
Uh, I don't really know that much about it.

03:26.539 --> 03:28.374
Tuesday
Daily Duties
Izumi Takaya
Okay, well I'll go see it for myself!

03:28.374 --> 03:29.742
Tuesday
Daily Duties
Izumi Takaya
Whoa! Hold on, Mayura!

03:29.742 --> 03:30.003
Whoa! Hold on, Mayura!

03:31.277 --> 03:33.404
What about your afternoon classes?

03:35.081 --> 03:36.412
She's gone...

03:44.257 --> 03:46.452
Pardon me.

03:58.404 --> 04:00.406
Oh, it's just a cat.

04:00.406 --> 04:02.374
C'mon, don't scare me like that!

04:25.632 --> 04:27.827
What an atmosphere!

04:30.803 --> 04:33.363
Hey, Mister Ghost! Are you in here?

04:33.973 --> 04:36.942
Hello? Special Delivery!

04:38.044 --> 04:40.512
I guess it won't show itself so easily.

04:49.656 --> 04:51.123
The doll?

04:53.626 --> 04:55.594
It laughed!

04:55.995 --> 04:57.326
Hey, Big Sis.

04:58.264 --> 04:59.561
It spoke!

05:00.633 --> 05:01.827
It... It flew!

05:13.146 --> 05:16.843
Mayura! Please explain how you met
this most unusual talking doll.

05:17.317 --> 05:18.685
Would the two of you smile, please?

05:18.685 --> 05:20.380
Please pose together!

05:22.922 --> 05:25.550
I could become famous in an instant.

05:30.296 --> 05:32.730
You don't seem bad or anything.

05:33.066 --> 05:35.193
Gimme a hug.

05:35.668 --> 05:37.135
Okay, sure!

05:39.505 --> 05:42.201
That makes me happy, Big Sis.

05:42.442 --> 05:44.410
Vengeful spirit, begone!

05:51.551 --> 05:53.746
The spirit has been dispelled.

05:55.288 --> 05:58.291
Things should completely turn around
for your company now.

05:58.291 --> 06:00.693
Oh, thank you so much!

06:00.693 --> 06:02.490
Think nothing of it.

06:03.363 --> 06:05.832
My sincerest thanks.

06:05.832 --> 06:06.958
It's nothing, really.

06:07.133 --> 06:10.002
There are no "vengeful spirits"
or anything like 'em.

06:10.002 --> 06:12.129
There's no such thing!

06:16.242 --> 06:17.573
She's home already?

06:18.111 --> 06:20.545
I'm telling you it's the truth!

06:20.747 --> 06:24.083
It speaks! And it's so cute when it smiles!

06:24.083 --> 06:26.051
I wasn't just seeing things!

06:27.120 --> 06:28.287
Ah, you're back.

06:28.287 --> 06:30.123
Hey, Dad. Yeah, I'm home.

06:30.123 --> 06:32.751
So I'll come over and show it to you, okay?

06:33.626 --> 06:35.253
On the phone, huh?

06:49.709 --> 06:51.310
Uh, I must be a little tired.

06:51.310 --> 06:52.845
Wonder if I've got any
energy drinks lying around.

06:52.845 --> 06:54.080
Yeah, okay!

06:54.080 --> 06:56.708
Four o'clock, at the usual place, right? Bye!

06:58.117 --> 06:59.652
What does she mean, "seeing things"?

06:59.652 --> 07:01.449
If she just saw for herself,
she'd agree with me!

07:03.322 --> 07:04.619
Hey!

07:06.292 --> 07:07.554
No, stop!

07:14.333 --> 07:18.463
Enjaku
Detective
Agency

07:18.638 --> 07:20.401
Where did it go?

07:21.441 --> 07:24.035
There's a detective agency here?

07:37.657 --> 07:39.192
I've brought your tea.

07:39.192 --> 07:41.490
Oh. Thanks, Yamino.

07:44.363 --> 07:46.499
Not getting any customers, are we?

07:46.499 --> 07:48.126
Actually, one's coming now.

07:50.503 --> 07:51.595
See?

07:53.506 --> 07:55.133
Yes, coming!

07:58.978 --> 08:00.146
Please, come in.

08:00.146 --> 08:01.147
SHMEJ MUSHROOMS

08:01.147 --> 08:02.842
The shimeji mushrooms have arrived.

08:03.015 --> 08:04.784
Straight from the farm!

08:04.784 --> 08:06.581
This "mail order" thing certainly
is convenient, no?

08:08.754 --> 08:10.051
Shimeji?

08:11.090 --> 08:12.580
You in there?

08:16.896 --> 08:18.693
Not here either.

08:27.106 --> 08:30.405
I guess I should go get help from a pro.

08:31.377 --> 08:32.111
Enjaku
Detective
Agency

08:32.111 --> 08:35.781
Enjaku
Detective
Agency
But I wonder if it's okay to trust them?

08:35.781 --> 08:36.382
Enjaku
Detective
Agency

08:36.382 --> 08:38.684
I mean, I can't even read the name.

08:38.684 --> 08:40.709
It's read "Enjaku Detective Agency."

08:48.194 --> 08:50.162
That guy's the detective?!

08:50.162 --> 08:51.959
He's, like, kinda cool.

08:52.064 --> 08:53.827
You're in need of our services, yes?

08:55.668 --> 08:58.137
And you have a request, don't you?
Please, step inside!

08:58.137 --> 09:00.367
Ah, well um... I mean, uh...

09:03.543 --> 09:06.746
Why don't we discuss things...

09:06.746 --> 09:08.873
over a nice, hot cup of tea?

09:15.321 --> 09:18.882
Um... Wait a minute, Mister Detective.

09:20.960 --> 09:23.588
Actually, I am not a detective.

09:29.869 --> 09:31.837
You have a client, Master Loki.

09:35.308 --> 09:37.410
Oh, little lost lamb...

09:37.410 --> 09:39.207
Welcome to my detective agency.

09:49.822 --> 09:51.016
Is something the matter?

09:51.824 --> 09:54.793
You're the detective?

09:55.528 --> 09:57.196
But you're still just a child!

09:57.196 --> 10:00.566
I'll have you know that this "receptacle" does
not necessarily reflect my true abilities.

10:00.566 --> 10:02.068
What is your name?

10:02.068 --> 10:04.804
Me? Mayura Daidoji.

10:04.804 --> 10:05.771
Mayura.

10:10.910 --> 10:13.546
So, Mayura. What can I help you with?

10:13.546 --> 10:17.243
Huh? Uh, well... There's something
I'd like you to look for.

10:17.583 --> 10:19.452
What's that?

10:19.452 --> 10:21.120
Um... a doll.

10:21.120 --> 10:22.388
A doll?

10:22.388 --> 10:23.489
Yeah.

10:23.489 --> 10:25.358
It laughs and talks and stuff!

10:25.358 --> 10:28.060
It goes, like, "Hee hee hee"
and "Hey, Big Sis."

10:28.060 --> 10:30.221
Oh, how cute!

10:32.298 --> 10:34.266
So, so cute!

10:34.734 --> 10:36.702
Yamino. Please see her out.

10:38.137 --> 10:42.096
What's his problem?! He asked me what
I was after, and I told him!

10:42.775 --> 10:44.072
Bleh!

10:46.345 --> 10:48.414
And here I thought we'd
finally gotten a client.

10:48.414 --> 10:50.439
Let's go, Yamino.

10:51.117 --> 10:53.119
Ah. So you're accepting her case?

10:53.119 --> 10:54.320
No.

10:54.320 --> 10:55.617
I felt it...

10:57.356 --> 11:00.519
A faint aura that she has
picked up somewhere.

11:02.361 --> 11:03.589
An aura of evil.

11:27.520 --> 11:28.782
What are those?

11:29.689 --> 11:32.749
Spectral search rods.
I bought them through mail order.

11:33.192 --> 11:34.727
Spectral search?

11:34.727 --> 11:38.431
Supposedly, they'll detect any ghosts
within a 10-meter radius.

11:38.431 --> 11:40.733
I'm sure they'll react to evil auras too.

11:40.733 --> 11:41.791
You believe that, huh?

11:42.968 --> 11:44.595
What do you mean?

11:45.705 --> 11:47.332
Oh, nothing.

11:50.843 --> 11:52.244
There, see? They're moving!

11:52.244 --> 11:53.142
No way!

11:58.884 --> 12:00.852
The signal's gone.

12:01.320 --> 12:03.447
I wonder if the source has moved.

12:04.390 --> 12:07.257
You think maybe it was picking up
the wrong thing to begin with?

12:12.431 --> 12:13.989
You there, Dolly?

12:16.702 --> 12:18.192
Not here either.

12:18.838 --> 12:20.135
Dolly!

12:23.342 --> 12:25.310
Oww...

12:33.352 --> 12:34.649
Come on already.

12:37.957 --> 12:39.125
Thanks.

12:39.125 --> 12:40.752
What kind of doll is it?

12:41.694 --> 12:44.322
I can't search for it if I don't
know what it looks like.

12:45.965 --> 12:49.093
I found the doll in this clock tower.

12:49.969 --> 12:53.639
A cat was here too, so I thought
maybe it brought the doll back.

12:53.639 --> 12:55.141
But it wasn't there.

12:55.141 --> 12:58.599
And then I thought, "Well, maybe it's
still around here somewhere."

12:59.545 --> 13:01.911
What on Earth has gotten into you?

13:02.314 --> 13:03.983
I'm already doing my own investigation, so...

13:03.983 --> 13:04.677
Whoa!

13:05.017 --> 13:06.985
What a reaction!

13:07.620 --> 13:09.918
That way! Let's go, Master Loki!

13:10.890 --> 13:12.324
Hey, wait!

13:12.324 --> 13:14.121
What about my doll?

13:16.495 --> 13:18.097
Fine, then!

13:18.097 --> 13:20.725
I'll find it on my own!

13:23.402 --> 13:24.391
That voice!

13:39.952 --> 13:41.253
There you are!

13:41.253 --> 13:42.955
We meet again, Big Sis.

13:42.955 --> 13:44.723
I guess you're all right, huh?

13:44.723 --> 13:46.350
I was so worried.

13:48.661 --> 13:50.185
I want to...

13:50.763 --> 13:52.390
go up there.

13:53.032 --> 13:54.567
The clock tower?

13:54.567 --> 13:57.069
I want to go up there with you.

13:57.069 --> 13:59.037
Okay. Then let's go up.

14:03.275 --> 14:05.744
As long as it's for Master Loki...

14:05.744 --> 14:07.871
Heave-ho! Heave-ho!

14:08.948 --> 14:10.040
Anything there?

14:10.783 --> 14:13.411
No, nothing yet.

14:15.955 --> 14:17.081
What happened?

14:17.590 --> 14:19.217
I hit something.

14:32.771 --> 14:36.537
Master Loki, I've done it!
It's a hot spring!

14:37.142 --> 14:40.373
Seems a little, uh, cold for
a hot spring, Yamino.

14:47.386 --> 14:50.014
What are you doing there?

14:54.426 --> 14:56.762
So you used to work at this mansion?

14:56.762 --> 15:00.299
Yes. Of course, that was 20 years ago.

15:00.299 --> 15:02.597
How did it end up like this?

15:04.403 --> 15:05.738
A fire.

15:05.738 --> 15:06.605
Fire?

15:06.605 --> 15:08.807
We don't know what caused it.

15:08.807 --> 15:12.265
But the flames had engulfed the
mansion in the blink of an eye.

15:14.179 --> 15:16.248
Was anyone caught in the blaze?

15:16.248 --> 15:17.875
The young mistress.

15:20.019 --> 15:22.317
She was such a sweet girl.

15:29.695 --> 15:31.263
We're here.

15:31.263 --> 15:33.561
I guess for you that means we're "home."

15:46.946 --> 15:48.681
A doll?

15:48.681 --> 15:51.483
Ah, that would be the one the
young mistress had.

15:51.483 --> 15:54.111
It was most precious to her.

15:54.253 --> 15:55.587
Is that right?

15:55.587 --> 15:58.223
So did it have some kind of device
that made it speak?

15:58.223 --> 16:00.693
Speak? That doll?

16:00.693 --> 16:03.161
Don't be ridiculous.

16:05.097 --> 16:08.794
Ma'am, did that bracelet also belong
to the young mistress?

16:09.101 --> 16:13.629
Yes. She was always wearing it.

16:14.006 --> 16:15.473
Let me see it a moment.

16:16.442 --> 16:17.409
Okay.

16:20.012 --> 16:21.113
Master Loki!

16:21.113 --> 16:22.171
Mayura!

16:32.992 --> 16:34.653
Big Sis...

16:49.541 --> 16:50.876
What's wrong?

16:50.876 --> 16:54.505
We're finally alone together.

16:55.781 --> 16:58.341
No! Stay away!

16:58.751 --> 17:02.388
Ah... So you don't like me anymore.

17:02.388 --> 17:04.379
That's why you left me behind, isn't it?

17:04.523 --> 17:05.858
What?

17:05.858 --> 17:07.485
What are you talking about?

17:16.268 --> 17:17.735
I can't forgive you!

17:18.270 --> 17:19.396
I can't forgive you!

17:40.859 --> 17:42.156
Loki!

17:50.869 --> 17:52.336
Don't interfere!

17:52.738 --> 17:55.140
This girl is not your owner.

17:55.140 --> 17:59.042
Your owner died 20 years ago,
in a fire at this mansion.

18:06.618 --> 18:07.812
You're a nuisance!

18:08.220 --> 18:09.346
Listen.

18:09.988 --> 18:12.157
You weren't abandoned.

18:12.157 --> 18:14.819
She didn't desert you. It's not like that.

18:15.461 --> 18:17.296
Until the very end, your master...

18:17.296 --> 18:18.464
Be quiet!

18:18.464 --> 18:20.261
I was abandoned.

18:20.999 --> 18:23.627
She decided she didn't like me anymore!

18:30.409 --> 18:32.877
It's been completely consumed by evil!

18:35.080 --> 18:36.206
Mayura!

18:46.625 --> 18:47.592
Master Loki!

18:48.127 --> 18:49.287
It's all right.

19:10.415 --> 19:11.712
Stay away!

19:12.851 --> 19:14.148
Stay away!

20:14.146 --> 20:15.443
Master Loki.

20:28.393 --> 20:30.520
You were lonely, weren't you?

20:42.975 --> 20:45.102
They're together now.

20:45.677 --> 20:47.144
She won't be lonely anymore.

20:59.258 --> 21:01.126
The clock!

21:01.126 --> 21:04.755
Time that was frozen is now moving again.

21:18.076 --> 21:19.978
This shimeji rice is the best!

21:19.978 --> 21:21.480
You're a genius, Yamino!

21:21.480 --> 21:23.382
Why, thank you.

21:23.382 --> 21:26.579
So... Why exactly are you here?

21:26.885 --> 21:28.920
Don't worry about the details!

21:28.920 --> 21:30.088
Oh, that's right!

21:30.088 --> 21:34.047
I've decided I'm going to start
helping out at this agency.

21:34.660 --> 21:35.957
What are you talking about?

21:36.428 --> 21:41.058
Well, it's like, if I'm here, I get the feeling
I'll run into a ton of strange mysteries.

21:41.833 --> 21:42.934
You know, Mayura,

21:42.934 --> 21:45.270
it's dangerous to go poking your nose
into things just because you're curious.

21:45.270 --> 21:47.205
Announcing the Beautiful Girl Detective!

21:47.205 --> 21:48.206
Oh, yeah!

21:48.206 --> 21:49.207
She's not listening.

21:49.207 --> 21:50.742
Yamino! Another bowl, please.

21:50.742 --> 21:52.577
And make it a big one, okay? A big one!

21:52.577 --> 21:55.414
Wow, I sure am going to be
busy from now on!

21:55.414 --> 21:56.848
Woo-hoo! Yeah!

21:56.848 --> 21:57.683
Master Loki?

21:57.683 --> 21:58.850
Yamino.

21:58.850 --> 22:00.613
I'll have another bowl too.

22:17.469 --> 22:29.438
A moonlit road pierces the dense fog

22:31.116 --> 22:42.861
Perplexedly, we all wander towards tomorrow

22:42.861 --> 22:50.068
We escape the darkness of a desolate town

22:50.068 --> 22:56.408
Which threatens to halt even the telling of myths

22:56.408 --> 23:05.917
Transcending the limitless skies,
we're on a journey

23:05.917 --> 23:10.255
Even if we're hurt

23:10.255 --> 23:22.267
We're sure we can still make it,
so we want to keep on praying

23:22.267 --> 23:23.996
Believe in Heaven

23:31.777 --> 23:32.310
Next Episode

23:32.310 --> 23:35.080
Next Episode
The next episode's keywords are, "school,"
"wooden sword," and "part-time job!"

23:35.080 --> 23:36.715
Next Episode
Wow! Now I'm psyched!

23:36.715 --> 23:38.083
Next Episode
Hey, wait a minute. Who are you?

23:38.083 --> 23:39.384
Next Episode
Ah, good question!

23:39.384 --> 23:41.186
Next Episode
But, that is the question! Who am I?

23:41.186 --> 23:43.188
Next Episode
Hmm... Gimme a hint!

23:43.188 --> 23:44.689
Next Episode
The first letter is "N."

23:44.689 --> 23:45.657
Next Episode
"N"? Nu... Naa...

23:45.657 --> 23:46.491
Next Episode
Nutcase!

23:46.491 --> 23:47.492
Next Episode
The first letter of my name!

23:47.492 --> 23:49.828
Next Episode
Huh? Narita Express!

23:49.828 --> 23:51.696
Next Episode
"The next stop is Tokyo..."

23:51.696 --> 23:52.864
Next Episode
"Please stand behind the yellow line..."

23:52.864 --> 23:55.267
Next Episode
D'oh! You made a monkey outta me!

23:55.267 --> 23:55.300
D'oh! You made a monkey outta me!

23:55.300 --> 23:56.001
The Mythical Detective Loki Ragnarok,

23:56.001 --> 23:57.068
The 2nd Night
The Allies of Justice are Totally Broke?!
The Mythical Detective Loki Ragnarok,

23:57.068 --> 23:58.870
The 2nd Night
The Allies of Justice are Totally Broke?!
"The Allies of Justice are Totally Broke?!"

23:58.870 --> 24:00.872
The 2nd Night
The Allies of Justice are Totally Broke?!
Sounds like another strange mystery!

24:00.872 --> 24:01.634
The 2nd Night
The Allies of Justice are Totally Broke?!
